#dig
(name *) excavation
(dict *) dig site 0n10e 0n 10e
(heads *) dig site
(room *)
(look *)
	Or as the archaeologists call it, 0N10E: zero meters north and ten meters east of the datum. This square has been excavated more than its neighbors, sinking it a few meters into the earth.
	(if) (eastern connection unlocked) (#looseearth is unvisited) (then)
		(par) It’s hard to keep your bearings between the real world and a memory, but those other remains should be somewhere to the east. Hopefully some of them are still there.
	(endif)
	(if) (northern connection unlocked) (#deeppit is unvisited) (then)
		(par) If those other bones were to the east, then the secret passage should be...due north.
	(endif)

(from * go #east to #looseearth) (eastern connection unlocked)
(from * go #north to #deeppit) (northern connection unlocked)
(from * go #west through #rope-u to #abovedig) (upper rope connected)
(from * go #west to #abovedig) ~(upper rope connected) %% Prevented
(from * go #up to #west)

(before [leave * #west])
	(#cart is #in *)
	(current player $Player)
	~($Player is #on #cart)
	(first try [enter #cart])

(prevent [leave * #west])
	~(upper rope connected)
	(current player $Player)
	~($Player is #on #cart)
	The datum is about three meters above the dig site, and the slope is steep. You’ll need some way to climb up.

%% There are many bones in this game
(name (bones $)) bone fragments
(dict (bones $)) bones fragment remains
(clarify location of *(bones $))
(when (bones $) is out of reach)
	Probably best not to touch the artifacts. Even if you’re an official guest of the dig team, you’re not a trained archaeologist, and there’s always the risk of contaminating something in the process.

#bones-n
(bones *)
(dict *) of nabuu-shumu-ishkun nabuu shumu ishkun
(* is #in #dig)
(* divines to #n-ziqqurat)
(descr *)
	There’s not much, just a few white glints in the moonlight
	(if) (#n-execution is unvisited) (then)
		...or is it just your imagination? There’s only one way to be sure: put your skills to the test and (link [divine the bones]) {divine them} .
	(else)
		: the remains of Nabuu-shumu-ishkun of Babylon.
	(endif)
(appearance *)
	(if) (#n-ziqqurat is unvisited) (then)
		According to the dig reports, these are the coordinates where human remains were found earlier today. With any luck, there should be some (vlink {bone fragments}) left to find.
	(else)
		You can just barely make out some (vlink {bone fragments}) in the moonlight.
	(endif)

#looseearth
(name *) loose earth
(dict *) 0n20e 0n 20e
(room *)
(look *) The square at 0N20E has been less thoroughly excavated than 0N10E, and the earth is softer here: the archaeologists have been working their way through it, breaking up each layer and sifting through the dirt for artifacts.

(from * go #west to #dig)
(from * go #northwest to #deeppit) (#deeppit is visited) %% Cleaner to only show the north-south connection on the map until it’s been explored, but after that it’s fine to allow NW-SE movement also

#bones-s
(bones *)
(dict *) of sharhiya sharhiya’s sharhiya's artifact artifacts latest finds
(* is #in #looseearth)
(* divines to #s-palace)
(descr *)
	Just a few white fragments among the artifacts—it’s hard to even tell which bones they are.
	(if) (#s-palace is unvisited) (then)
		Could they belong to the Sharhiya from the memories?
	(else)
		But they’re certainly Sharhiya’s.
	(endif)
(appearance *)
	The (vlink {latest finds}) have been carefully sorted and labelled in trays off to one side
	(if) (#s-palace is visited) (then)
		(no space) —including the bones of Sharhiya of Babylon
	(endif)
	.

